{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-23T07:56:56.268Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"cf73d9707128820a198a2441","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/6","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-23T07:56:56.267Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Reopened for PR 99 blocking review. Confirmed two root gaps in the previous head: semantically inconsistent original receipts could pass hash/history checks, and reloaded manifests bypassed cohort and both-arm allowance checks. Fix will use shared manifest and receipt validators for observation, resume, comparison and the authoritative promotion gate. Validation will bind actions to consented input/policy tables, enforce finite bounded and same-action-consistent rewards, verify disagreement/failure/digest fields, and check actual unique receipt charges against both allowances. Four requested adversarial regressions and independent behavioral revert proofs will be recorded; no review-thread replies or mentions."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-23T07:56:56.268Z"}],"before_hash":"462aa3c45f6e2bb85736f827bf80030038fb41d372a30417957ad9b0a68aac1f","after_hash":"2b7469ba2b5142af1ce801655013e7dfdb491f9e44a9b10f3b29820f700bcaf2","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"0c33753c5540c565473d2ed3ab774b914001fa125848a50c4859c5eba2509a59"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-23T08:16:19.060Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"cf73d9707128820a198a2441","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/7","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-23T08:16:19.060Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Both blocking review findings are fixed through shared validators. validateDeployment now governs registration and every manifest reload: generation pair, exact plan cohort, consent, both reserved allowances and actual receipt inventory charges; extra slots cannot hide outside report counts. validateObservation now governs live observation, retry/resume, comparison and promotion reads: policy-produced actions for the consented input, bounded rewards, same-action reward equality, disagreement/failure flags and selected-outcome digest. Refusals use pinned SDK context.item_id and context.field and include both in the message. Focused suite passes 25/25 with 100% shadow lines/branches/functions. Four independent behavioral reverts each fail 1/1 with Missing expected rejection: identical-action rewards, zero-budget original manifest, tampered disagreement, and cohort expansion after plan registration; validators restored. Broader original-record tests also cover wrong actions, bounds, digests, slot IDs, unexpected charged receipts, both aggregate charges, edited manifests and native SDK workflow-policy refusal. No SDK mocks, history rewriting, dependency bumps, review-thread replies or mentions."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-23T08:16:19.060Z"}],"before_hash":"2b7469ba2b5142af1ce801655013e7dfdb491f9e44a9b10f3b29820f700bcaf2","after_hash":"8b64a4088224bf77f48234005cd043f5299746539ece25d729f187d479e600d7","item_hash_version":3